# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI KEYS GO HERE (server side only). They are never put in the app.
# Copy this file to "supabase/.env", paste your key(s), then run:
#   npx supabase secrets set --env-file supabase/.env
# The file supabase/.env is git-ignored and never ships in the app.
#
# Do NOT add the Supabase service_role key or any name starting with SUPABASE_ here:
# Supabase provides those to the functions itself, and refuses them in "secrets set".
# Check this file any time (prints no secrets):  npm run check:env
#
# For AI, you only NEED the Gemini key. ChatGPT and Claude are optional:
# the app shows each one as "Connected" only when its key is set here.
# Apple subscriptions also require REVENUECAT_SECRET_API_KEY (see below).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Required. Get it at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=PASTE-YOUR-GEMINI-API-KEY-HERE
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# Optional: ChatGPT (OpenAI). Get a key at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# Leave the line out (or empty) to keep ChatGPT turned off.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.5

# Optional: Claude (Anthropic). Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/
# Leave the line out (or empty) to keep Claude turned off.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# Required to verify Apple subscriptions on the server (never put this key in the app).
# Create a RevenueCat secret API key with subscriber-read access.
# REVENUECAT_SECRET_API_KEY=
# Must match the App Store Connect product IDs and RevenueCat entitlements.
# REVENUECAT_PLUS_PRODUCT_ID=turzam_plus_monthly
# REVENUECAT_PRO_PRODUCT_ID=turzam_pro_monthly
# REVENUECAT_PLUS_ENTITLEMENT_ID=turzam_plus
# REVENUECAT_PRO_ENTITLEMENT_ID=turzam_pro

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional cost controls. The defaults are already safe; change only if you need to.
# After editing run again: npx supabase secrets set --env-file supabase/.env
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Longest visible answer, in tokens (256 to 16000). Default 4096.
# MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=4096
# How hard Gemini 3.x thinks: low (default, cheapest), medium or high. "Deep Think" mode always uses high.
# GEMINI_THINKING_LEVEL=low
# Per-user limits. kind = CHAT, SEARCH, AUX (titles, memory, ideas), TRANSCRIBE
# Defaults: CHAT 12/min 150/day, SEARCH 6/min 40/day, AUX 30/min 400/day, TRANSCRIBE 10/min 100/day
# LIMIT_CHAT_PER_MINUTE=12
# LIMIT_CHAT_PER_DAY=150
# Free users may send this many AI chats before a fixed six-hour cooldown (default 10).
# Paid tiers bypass that cooldown and retain the existing per-minute safety limit.
# FREE_CHAT_LIMIT=10
# Paid rolling-24-hour chat quotas. Plus defaults to the existing CHAT daily cap (150); Pro defaults to 500.
# LIMIT_PLUS_CHAT_PER_DAY=150
# LIMIT_PRO_CHAT_PER_DAY=500
# LIMIT_SEARCH_PER_DAY=40
# LIMIT_TRANSCRIBE_PER_DAY=100
# Optional hard cap on calls per day across ALL users (a safety net against many fake accounts).
# Leave out to turn it off. Example: stop at 3000 chats per day in total.
# GLOBAL_CHAT_PER_DAY=3000
# GLOBAL_SEARCH_PER_DAY=500
# GLOBAL_TRANSCRIBE_PER_DAY=1000
